# Find the robot on the currently loaded map with no pose hint -- the
# recovery for a kidnapped robot (carried somewhere, booted away from its
# [initial_pose], or localization lost). Served by localizer_node
# (the workspace's syncai_localizer) on the relative name `auto_localize`, in
# the bare robot_id namespace, so it lands on <robot_id>/auto_localize, next to
# relocalize / relocalize_check. New in 2026-10. The backend called it behind
# POST /api/v1/localization/auto until 2026-10-15; that route now calls
# ResetOdometry with skip_seed, which runs this same search on the scans of a
# freshly reset Point-LIO (see the divergence note below).
#
# SUCCESS IS A RESULT, NOT A RECEIPT -- the opposite of Relocalize. The call
# blocks until either:
#   1. a global search over the map's poses.txt keyframes x a yaw sweep,
#      scored coarse-to-fine with GICP and checked for ambiguity, has found a
#      pose, AND
#   2. the localizer's own timer, handed that pose as its next guess, has
#      registered against a fresh scan (what IsValid / relocalize_check
#      reports as valid right after).
# Each half has its own deadline (the node's auto_loc.search_timeout_sec and
# auto_loc.converge_timeout_sec, 10 s + 5 s by default), so a caller's client
# timeout must exceed their sum. A failure in either half leaves localization
# as it was: the candidate is withdrawn and the timer goes back to its
# previous offset rather than retrying a guess that did not converge.
#
# It only works on a map saved with save_patches (the keyframe poses in
# map/<name>/poses.txt are the candidate positions), and it fails rather than
# guesses when two distinct poses score alike (a symmetric corridor). If the
# kidnap made Point-LIO itself diverge, this service cannot help: its scan
# window is posed by the diverged odometry. Call ResetOdometry instead (robot
# stationary), which resets the LIO, drops that window and ends in this same
# search when asked to (global_fallback, or skip_seed to go to it directly).
#
# No request fields: the whole point is that no hint is needed.
---
bool success
# Why it failed (no map, no poses.txt, ambiguous, timed out, did not
# converge), or a summary of the match.
string message
# The pose found, map frame, at the scan the search used. Angles in radians.
# Filled on success, and also on a convergence failure (the candidate that
# did not converge), for diagnosis; zero otherwise.
float32 x
float32 y
float32 z
float32 yaw
# Refine-stage pcl::Registration::getFitnessScore() of the winner (mean
# squared nearest-neighbour distance, m^2).
float32 fitness
# Fraction of the winner's refine-resolution scan points within the inlier
# distance of the map after alignment -- the search's acceptance gate.
float32 inlier_ratio
# How many (position, yaw) candidates the coarse stage scored.
int32 candidates
